<title>ESTONIA: ESTONIA - NOON HEADLINES - APRIL 8.</title>
<headline>ESTONIA - NOON HEADLINES - APRIL 8.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>These were the headlines on Estonian Kuku radio at Noon. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy.</p>
<p>- Norway invited U.S. Secretary of State Madeleine Albright to discuss the security of the Baltic countries.</p>
<p>- A captain of a Latvian fishing boat was reprimanded by the Latvian authorities after he illegal crossed the Estonian-Latvian sea border.</p>
<p>- A tunnel between Helsinki and Tallinn will cost 21.5 billion kroons, according to a preliminary project.</p>
<p>-- Tallinn newsroom, +372 6308 400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
